{"title":"Subjectwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electric Circuit","fileName":"027_Subjectwise Test-1 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Electric Circuit.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following circuit:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a6a24238246552f708b6171911d89291001b2ddd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Which of the following statement is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Power dissipated in 4 Ω resistance is 549.3 W.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Power dissipated in 1 Ω resistance is 61.03 W.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> Power dissipated in 30 Ω resistance is 173.20 W.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Power dissipated in 1 kΩ resistance is 91.4 W.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9b4bd8a4ac7b22166c022436a0b4291e0e26692d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Five capacitors <em>C</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>C</em><sub>2</sub>, <em>C</em><sub>3</sub>, <em>C</em><sub>4</sub> and <em>C</em><sub>5</sub> whose values are 3 μF, 2 μF, 2 μF, 4 μF, 5 μF have breakdown voltages of 15 V, 6 V, 4 V, 2 V and 3 V, respectively. As the network connection shown below, the maximum safe voltage that can be applied across the combination and the corresponding total charge in μC stored in the effective capacitance across the terminals are</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5cf7cf2db7b9d1108dcaac2d7f1557757edba2af.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 21.77 V and 80.31 μC</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 11.6 V and 42.8 μC</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<d