 <img src=\"/media/9bffa6cce677b679dd01a89c3abe3b4451dd56b0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The voltage <img src=\"/media/2272bbf687a081e0a551d3dee27cec34e06c861c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> then the value of current supplied by the source is equal to</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n 5 cos(ω<em>t</em>) A</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n cos (ω<em>t</em> + 45°) A</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n 2 sin (ω<em>t</em> – 45°) A</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5f6551fdf385aa73f7b0965186f7c6436330cc8f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/04797369901a6d18ab2b8075edfe702e2230dbf4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n A series <em>RLC</em> network with <em>R</em> = 5 Ω, <em>L</em> = 0.1 H and <em>C</em> = 500 μF has a constant voltage <em>V</em> = 10 Volts applied at <em>t</em> = 0. Which of the following statements regarding the series <em>RLC</em> circuit is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n The resonant frequency of the circuit is ω<em><sub>r</sub></em> = 141.42 rad/sec.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n At ω<em><sub>r</sub></em> capacitor voltage <img src=\"/media/bca336e73722b0e463484b866b72a99a0a2a4e98.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The Q-factor of the circuit is 2.828.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n The phase difference at resonance between capacitor voltage <em>V<sub>C</sub></em> and inductor voltage <em>V<sub>L</sub></em> is 180°.</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, b, c, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/09c83f406d29